{"Title":"An Act relative to auto insurance costs for traditionally low-and moderate income communities ","BillNumber":"H1098","DocketNumber":"HD480","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"FAM1","Name":"Frank A. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/FAM1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T11:17:51.737"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"FAM1","Name":"Frank A. Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/FAM1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T11:17:51.7366667"},{"Id":"EAR1","Name":"Estela A. Reyes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/EAR1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T14:00:24.91"},{"Id":"FEP1","Name":"Francisco E. Paulino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/FEP1","ResponseDate":"2023-11-15T12:40:11.04"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1098/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Moran of Lawrence, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1098) of Frank A. Moran and Estela A. Reyes relative to motor vehicle insurance costs for traditionally low-and moderate income communities.  Financial Services.","DocumentText":"\tThe commissioner of insurance shall conduct an investigation and study of the impact of geographic location data in automobile insurance rate calculation. The commissioner shall evaluate, at a minimum: (1) the automobile insurance premiums for each zip code in the commonwealth; (2) the difference in automobile insurance premiums for drivers with equivalent driving factors, such as accidents and miles driven per year, in low income, moderate income, and high income zip codes; (3) the risk factors for each zip code in the commonwealth; and (4) the discriminatory impact on drivers in low and moderate income zip codes. The commissioner shall make recommendations and shall submit findings to the joint committee on transportation and to the house and senate committees on ways and means not later than December 31, 2024. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J11","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J11"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}